r314 (2026-10-04, b70 lab, NOT BUILT): let the GDN speculative kernels take a row-strided state-index tensor.

Applies on vllm-xpu-kernels 6d92b1b + r310 + r313 (only gdn_attn_interface.cpp, compiled into _xpu_C; rebuild like
docker/rebase-v0290/build-kernels-0.1.14.1-r313-spec-exact.sh). Pair it with the research overlay
experiments/qwen38-27b-b70/overlays/b70-gdn-state-width (B70_GDN_STATE_WIDTH=1), which hands the kernel a
[n, step width] view of [n, num_spec + 1] block-table rows when a step is narrower than num_spec + 1.

Why: after a verify step accepts `a` tokens, the next step's SSM spec kernel reads its initial state from
spec_state_indices_tensor[n, a - 1] (gated_delta_rule.hpp:392-395) with no bound check, but the engine slices that
tensor to the next step's width (vllm gdn_attn.py:338-340 / 359-361). Narrower next step => out-of-range read.
The width cannot simply be made larger: both spec kernels and the interface take the number of tokens per request
from size(1) (gdn_attn_interface.cpp:96 and :119, gated_delta_rule.hpp:705, causal_conv1d.hpp:1039). They already
address elements through stride(0) (gated_delta_rule.hpp:395 and :511, causal_conv1d.hpp:681), so a strided view
keeps size(1) = tokens per request and still exposes columns up to num_spec. The only obstacle is the
is_contiguous() check, relaxed here to "rows contiguous". Every contiguous tensor still passes, with the same
kernel arguments, so nothing changes for the stock engine.
--- a/csrc/xpu/gdn_attn/gdn_attn_interface.cpp
+++ b/csrc/xpu/gdn_attn/gdn_attn_interface.cpp
@@ -79,9 +79,20 @@
       "spec_token_indx must be 1D of shape [spec_token]");
   const int spec_token = spec_token_indx.size(0);
 
+  // r314 (b70 lab): rows may be strided. size(1) is still the number of tokens
+  // per request in this step (num_speculative_tokens + 1 below), but the row
+  // stride may be wider: the conv and SSM spec kernels address every element
+  // as cache_indices[n * stride(0) + col] (causal_conv1d.hpp, gated_delta_rule.hpp)
+  // and read the initial SSM state from col num_accepted_tokens[n] - 1, which
+  // can lie past size(1) when this step is narrower than the previous step's
+  // acceptance. The engine passes a [n, width] view of [n, num_spec + 1]
+  // block-table rows for that case; a contiguous tensor is unchanged.
   TORCH_CHECK(
-      spec_state_indices_tensor.is_contiguous(),
-      "spec_state_indices_tensor must be contiguous");
+      spec_state_indices_tensor.stride(1) == 1 &&
+          spec_state_indices_tensor.stride(0) >=
+              spec_state_indices_tensor.size(1),
+      "spec_state_indices_tensor rows must be contiguous (stride(1) == 1, "
+      "stride(0) >= size(1))");
   TORCH_CHECK(
       spec_state_indices_tensor.dtype() == torch::kInt32,
       "spec_state_indices_tensor must be of int32 dtype");
